    {
      "id": "distonyc-1d7840d9c9addba07ccabdb2",
      "title": "Blood on My Shoes at Daybreak",
      "url": "https://github.com/legauntt/yehry3/releases/download/distonyc-v1/distonyc-1d7840d9c9addba07ccabdb2-043701a808ad.mp3",
      "duration": 241.74,
      "collection": "distonyc",
      "lyrics": {
        "text": "[Intro — muttered, then sung]\nWhich shoe's mine? Both? That's unfortunate.\nThere was snow where my house used to stand.\nNow there's something asleep in the cellar,\nAnd an axe getting warm in my hand.\n\n[Verse 1]\nI came from the north with a name in my teeth,\nWith the names of my dead underneath.\nThrough the dungeon's mouth, down the wet stone throat,\nPast a priest in a butcher's coat.\nHe said, kneel down, son, there's a power below.\nI said, these shoes don't bend that low.\nTook a drink for the courage I already had,\nSpilled the rest on the stair. Waste of that.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nSomething wearing a man's face smiled.\nI remembered the face of my child.\nHeld my breath till the shaking passed;\nThen I asked which prayer would be its last.\n\n[Chorus]\nBlood on my shoes, dawn in my eyes,\nI've got one more dark thing to outlive tonight.\nCall me a god if it helps you sleep;\nI'm a man with a promise I mean to keep.\nOpen the shutters, uncover the light.\nSomething that hunted you died tonight.\nBlood on my shoes, mud on the floor;\nYou won't hear that scratching anymore.\n\n[Verse 2]\nAncient streets underneath the ground,\nAll that glory with nobody round.\nI walked where the hungry reached up for a crown;\nKept my own two feet coming down.\nGold makes a terrible boot, you know.\nTry running in that through the northern snow.\nHa—my left shoe's talking. It says we're through.\nMy right says there's work we've still got to do.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nLet the great ones bargain for endless years.\nI've had plenty of time with fear.\nThere's a trail from this pit to the world outside,\nAnd I'm following every stride.\n\n[Chorus]\nBlood on my shoes, dawn in my eyes,\nI've got one more dark thing to outlive tonight.\nCall me a god if it helps you sleep;\nI'm a man with a promise I mean to keep.\nOpen the shutters, uncover the light.\nSomething that hunted you died tonight.\nBlood on my shoes, mud on the floor;\nYou won't hear that scratching anymore.\n\n[Bridge — half-time, exposed melody]\nBottle's empty. Keep it still.\nFor a second I can see our windowsill.\nLittle shoes drying beside the flame—\nDon't make a chorus out of their names.\nLet me hold them where the noise can't reach.\nLet the silence finish what I can't speak.\nThen lace these boots with a steady hand.\nThere's another village beyond this land.\n\n[Final Chorus — rising intensity]\nBlood on my shoes, dawn in my eyes,\nI brought something mortal through endless night.\nGod of Ultra Violence, that's what they'll say;\nI want children to walk home safe.\nOpen the shutters, uncover the light.\nSomething that hunted you died tonight.\nBlood on my shoes, mud on the floor;\nYou won't hear that scratching anymore.\n\n[Outro — gently sung]\nAt the last house, I leave them outside,\nThose terrible shoes with the broken ties.\nMorning comes. No claws at the door.\nI set down the axe.\nSleep on. I'll keep watch.",
        "kind": "written"
      },
      "collections": [
        "distonyc",
        "fearhunger"
      ]
    },
